From d01cba3b76f6e835b4e18a6d4cda7b29066e3a80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:13:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 15/26] ling: the latent caches split by 512-key chunks over
 two ranks past the native window (TF_LING_KV_SPLIT=auto|on|off): each rank
 keeps every other chunk (cache writes through main's page table, other ranks'
 rows to a spare page), runs every head's attention over its chunks (absorbed
 queries all-gathered), merges them per head in fp32 (tf_ling_merge_part,
 tf_glm_merge's loop as a template), swaps the other rank's heads' partials
 and merges the two with tf_glm_merge; tf_ling_chunks_split_r16 is
 tf_ling_chunks_r16's chunk kernel with a rank's chunk stride. Off: the
 launches are today's. Also: the prompt pass's logits and head gather sized
 for the one row it reads (0.72 GiB a rank at TP=2), and a kept prompt state
 holds the conv windows and each KDA layer's committed state only (0.31 ->
 0.14 GiB a rank). ling-tp: --prompt, --capacity, --resume (resumed == fresh);
 kernel contract: the split pair beside tf_ling_chunks_r16

